  "summary": "Elkton resident Zach Caudle recounts his effort to oppose Flock ALPR cameras in his town and alleges retaliation by the Rockingham County Sheriff's Office, including two traffic stops by the same deputy after he filed FOIA requests and the town voted 5-0 to cancel its Flock contract. He describes filing a formal complaint after the second stop and notes the Sheriff's Office deployed Flock cameras without a Board of Supervisors vote or public hearing.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Shortly after the Town of Elkton voted 5-0 to cancel its Flock contract, I learned that the Sheriff\u2019s Office was gearing up to use the system, even as its local partners were getting rid of the technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Sheriff\u2019s Office\u2019s own written response confirmed that no meetings were held with any county board before the cameras went up. There was no Board of Supervisors vote and no public hearing.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
